© 2024 Synopsys, Inc. 5RX PI input skew calibration algorithm – Input Skew 
Correction 
•Skew Correction is performed in the following steps: 
1. Sample the incoming loopback sinewave using 
skew correlation measurements (e21, e31, e41). 
–Each measurement samples the relative phase position of clk90, 180, or 270 relative to their quadrature neighbors. 
–Each phase is compared in case one phase is landing on portion of signal that doesn’t have significant p hase 
information (peak/trough rather than edge) 
2. Skew measurements are sampled and fed 
through an accumulator to average out noise. 
3. The resultant skew is collected at PI code 0 
(phase offset 0) and 64 (phase offset 90) and compared. 
4. If skew measurements are the same for PI code 0 
and 64, skew code is found, otherwise keep stepping the code until it is. 
